course: dictionary
lesson: 13612
title: Words that show no end
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Indefinitely is an adverb. It tells you how long something goes on: for a time with no fixed end. «The swimming pool is closed indefinitely.» Nobody can say which day it will open, so the notice gives no end date.
explain: Look at the words near it for clues. Closed, postponed and continue often sit next to indefinitely. «The school trip has been postponed indefinitely.» Postponed means moved to a later time, and indefinitely tells us that later time is not known. Check your meaning by swapping in "for a time with no set end" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Maths uses the word too. «The pattern of dots can continue indefinitely.» The dots never stop, so there is no last dot. The word does not give a number. It only tells us that no end has been planned.
fact: Indefinitely means for a time that has no fixed end.
fact: Nobody knows when something that is closed indefinitely will open again.
fact: Clues that often appear with it are closed, postponed, suspended and continue.
fact: A good check is to swap in "with no set end" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Indefinitely can also mean in an unclear or uncertain way, but this is rare in everyday reading.
exercise: «The library is closed indefinitely while the roof is mended.» What does indefinitely mean here? | Only at night | Very quickly | For exactly one day | *For a time with no fixed end
exercise: «The bus service has been suspended indefinitely.» What does the word indefinitely tell us? | It ends at noon | It is the name of the bus company | *It has no fixed end date | It runs twice a week
exercise: «The lights in the hall will stay on indefinitely.» Which swap keeps the same meaning? | Only for a short while | *With no set end | Without any electricity | Very brightly
test: «The park gates are locked indefinitely.» Which swap keeps the meaning? | On the first day of spring | *For an unknown length of time | For exactly ten minutes | Very loudly
test: «The pattern of stars can go on indefinitely.» What does this tell us? | It is very small | It is made of paper | It stops at ten | *It has no planned end
exam: «The match has been postponed indefinitely, so nobody knows when it will be played.» What does indefinitely show? | The match is finished | The match was cancelled because of rain | The match starts in five minutes | *There is no set end, so the new date is not known
